WEBVTT

00:00:03.060 --> 00:00:07.610
"Kashiga Beach Fireworks Festival"
"Spectacular flowers bloom above the ocean"
"7:00 PM on August 20"

00:00:03.770 --> 00:00:07.610
So let's ask Hotaru to come too,
and we'll all go together!

00:00:07.730 --> 00:00:09.150
We'll meet up at five, okay?

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:11.360
Fireworks...

00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:14.780
Hey, are you listening, Coconuts?!

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.530
Oh, sorry. Yeah, I'm listening.

00:00:16.530 --> 00:00:18.380
Are you sure? Geez...

00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.080
Well then, I'll see you there at five.
Could you call Hotaru?

00:00:23.080 --> 00:00:25.170
Sure, I will.

00:00:23.830 --> 00:00:26.330
"Entrance"

00:00:25.170 --> 00:00:27.290
But well, if I just wait, I think...

00:00:28.170 --> 00:00:32.000
...she'll show... up... here.

00:00:37.590 --> 00:00:46.100
"Ice"

00:00:38.140 --> 00:00:40.640
Um... I'll tell her about it.

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:42.060
What? Oh, she's there?

00:00:42.560 --> 00:00:44.590
Yeah. Later, then.

00:00:46.810 --> 00:00:49.570
Excuse me, Hotaru. What're you doing?

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:50.460
Shh!

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.160
I'm concentrating right now.

00:00:54.610 --> 00:00:56.360
O-Okay.

00:01:14.050 --> 00:01:15.960
I'd like to buy this one, please.

00:01:17.890 --> 00:01:21.680
"Ice"

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:21.280
Err... Okay.

00:01:22.770 --> 00:01:27.530
Homerun Bar... It is, needless to say,
an ice cream bar.

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:33.780
This is a product created by improving
upon the first ice cream bar in Japan.

00:01:34.400 --> 00:01:38.690
Also, this is Japan's first ice cream that
gives you the chance to win another one.

00:01:39.700 --> 00:01:44.700
Some of the bars have homeruns
or hits carved into their sticks.

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:42.330
"Meito Homerun! (Won 1 free bar)"
"Triple (3 points)"
"Double (2 points)" "Single (1 point)"

00:01:44.700 --> 00:01:49.290
Aside from the free bar that you can
still win today, I heard that in the past

00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:54.090
"Homerun Bar"

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:52.590
there were times when you
could win various prizes.

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:54.090
That's so generous!

00:01:56.840 --> 00:02:00.590
Oh, I see. You were so serious because
you wanted to win a homerun--

00:02:00.590 --> 00:02:04.640
Wha...?! I am always serious 
when I pick things!

00:02:04.640 --> 00:02:06.600
I-I see.

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:15.700
But, well... I guess...
I was exceptionally... serious.

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:19.610
Why is that?

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:34.220
I-I hope you win.

00:02:35.050 --> 00:02:39.010
Oh? But isn't it better for
the shop if I don't win?

00:02:39.010 --> 00:02:40.720
You'd be giving me one for free, you know.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:44.510
Whether you win or not, when we
get them from the manufacturer,

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.430
the number of winners is already decided,

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:50.100
so we don't lose anything by giving
one in exchange for a winning bar.

00:02:51.600 --> 00:02:55.010
That's true... You truly are an
exceptional shop tender, Kokonotsu.

00:02:55.520 --> 00:03:00.530
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:03.980
Oh, shoot!

00:03:05.160 --> 00:03:06.260
What's wrong?

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.540
The bus is gonna leave soon, so...

00:03:09.870 --> 00:03:13.290
Oh, you have to go somewhere? I'm sorry.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:17.300
Well, it's not like that.
I forgot to tell you this...

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.550
...but there's a fireworks festival
at the beach today.

00:03:20.220 --> 00:03:24.510
So... I wanted to ask you
if you'd be interested.

00:03:31.980 --> 00:03:33.080
Just the two of us?

00:03:33.730 --> 00:03:34.400
What?

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:41.990
"Meito Ho..."

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:46.100
Ah!

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.750
This isn't good. The next bus won't come...

00:03:53.540 --> 00:03:55.600
...for another two hours.

00:04:02.970 --> 00:04:04.210
Just the two of us?

00:04:05.930 --> 00:04:09.100
Kokonotsu... Kokonotsu...!

00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:11.070
Hey, you're getting tired!

00:04:11.640 --> 00:04:12.510
Right.

00:04:13.390 --> 00:04:15.850
The fireworks are starting soon!

00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:20.780
Hang in there! Kokonotsu!

00:04:29.540 --> 00:04:30.820
Coconuts isn't answering?

00:04:31.410 --> 00:04:32.370
No.

00:04:32.710 --> 00:04:34.660
I wonder if something happened.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:38.170
I'm sure they're fine.

00:04:38.420 --> 00:04:42.380
But with such a large crowd,
we may not be able to meet up.

00:04:44.090 --> 00:04:44.860
Yeah.

00:04:52.770 --> 00:04:53.370
Well...

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:58.240
...It may just be that he didn't notice
the call because they're on their way.

00:04:59.060 --> 00:05:00.400
I'm sure it'll all work out.

00:05:09.030 --> 00:05:11.580
Is this really gonna work out?!

00:05:12.040 --> 00:05:13.960
Kokonotsu, are you okay?

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:17.210
Yes...! Actually, I don't know!

00:05:19.170 --> 00:05:20.250
Also...

00:05:23.210 --> 00:05:24.290
Just the two of us?

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.470
Oh, no, it won't be just us.

00:05:27.470 --> 00:05:31.390
We're meeting with Saya and To, so the
four of us will go see them together.

00:05:32.430 --> 00:05:34.920
We decided to ask you if
you wanted to come, too.

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:38.940
Yes.

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:44.940
Why did I say that?!

00:05:52.790 --> 00:05:54.120
Hm?

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:58.350
What?!

00:06:01.750 --> 00:06:02.380
Let's...

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:04.920
...take a little break.

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:07.420
O-Okay.

00:06:13.220 --> 00:06:15.590
I'm a bit relieved...

00:06:16.930 --> 00:06:19.940
...because I can use this time
to tell her the truth.

00:06:20.900 --> 00:06:23.520
Um... To tell you the truth, today...

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.650
I'm sorry... for causing you distress.

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:28.390
What? Well...

00:06:30.240 --> 00:06:33.410
I wanted to talk with you
alone for a bit today.

00:06:33.620 --> 00:06:34.620
What?

00:06:34.620 --> 00:06:39.150
Thanks to you, I was able to learn how
I should be and how to look at things.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.940
Those two at Café Endo helped me, too.

00:06:44.040 --> 00:06:46.060
Every day was a brand-new experience.

00:06:46.920 --> 00:06:49.510
I've never spent a fun
summer break like this before.

00:06:50.380 --> 00:06:54.080
I'm having so much fun, 
too... Well, I mean...

00:06:56.140 --> 00:07:00.100
It may now have very little to do
with my purpose at the beginning.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:05.020
Right now, I want to talk with you alone.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:06.440
What...?

00:07:11.530 --> 00:07:12.530
Hota--

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:22.330
Oh, that's right... They're displaying
the fireworks over the ocean.

00:07:22.330 --> 00:07:24.230
We can see the ocean from here, so...

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:26.710
Cool!

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:33.530
So they've already started.
I have to apologize to those two later.

00:07:34.970 --> 00:07:36.310
Kokonotsu.

00:07:37.640 --> 00:07:38.560
This...

00:07:39.060 --> 00:07:40.980
Hm...? This is...

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.690
Whoa! You won! This is a
Homerun Bar winning stick!

00:07:43.560 --> 00:07:47.320
"Meito Homerun!"

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:50.650
What?! So you actually won?! YOU?!

00:07:50.650 --> 00:07:53.200
When you've never won no matter what you--

00:07:55.200 --> 00:07:58.580
I've never told you this before,
but I'm quite forgetful.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:03.140
So... you hold onto this...

00:08:04.880 --> 00:08:06.450
...so that I won't lose it.

00:08:21.560 --> 00:08:26.360
By doing this, next time I suddenly
want to eat a Homerun Bar,

00:08:26.360 --> 00:08:30.380
I'll feel as if I'm getting it for free.

00:08:34.410 --> 00:08:40.370
"Thump, thump, thump..."

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.070
I thought she was gonna kiss me!
I thought she was gonna kiss me...!

00:08:37.070 --> 00:08:39.830
I thought she was gonna kiss me!
I thought she was gonna kiss me!

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:40.840
Oh, that's right.

00:08:41.540 --> 00:08:47.410
Could you apologize to the other two
for me keeping you to myself.

00:08:56.590 --> 00:08:57.950
I think I'm going home now.

00:09:00.140 --> 00:09:01.190
Goodbye.

00:09:17.030 --> 00:09:18.650
It rained that day.

00:09:19.990 --> 00:09:23.320
So I thought that was the reason.

00:09:24.330 --> 00:09:29.630
"Shikada Dagashi"

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:27.180
No one likes to get wet in the rain.

00:09:31.460 --> 00:09:36.120
It rained the next day again.
So the reason was clear.

00:09:40.390 --> 00:09:42.350
Let me get out of this rain!

00:09:43.850 --> 00:09:45.100
Oh, hi, Saya.

00:09:45.310 --> 00:09:47.440
I'll go get a towel for you.

00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:48.540
Thank you.

00:09:52.270 --> 00:09:55.610
After that day, we had 
sunny days for a while...

00:10:47.450 --> 00:10:53.420
"Homerun Bar, Fireworks Festival, and..."

00:10:57.670 --> 00:10:59.760
Oh, hi, Coconuts.

00:11:00.470 --> 00:11:02.590
Would you like it iced or hot?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:05.580
Coconuts?

00:11:05.930 --> 00:11:09.780
Ah... Let's see... Iced then.

00:11:11.480 --> 00:11:12.350
Okay!

00:11:19.860 --> 00:11:20.850
Thanks.

00:11:21.360 --> 00:11:23.450
What, are you already going home?

00:11:23.450 --> 00:11:25.620
Yeah, I have to look after the shop, so...

00:11:26.200 --> 00:11:29.750
By the way, I haven't seen Hotaru lately.

00:11:31.500 --> 00:11:33.090
Is she out of town right now?

00:11:40.260 --> 00:11:41.430
I don't know.

00:11:59.150 --> 00:12:00.510
Summer is about to be over.

00:12:03.530 --> 00:12:04.430
And...

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:07.220
...winter will be here soon.

00:12:07.950 --> 00:12:16.510
"Next time:
Ambulance, Get a Move On, You Cod!, and..."
